# 8. Assistant Behavior for MarketData

When modifying MarketDataCore components, assistants MUST:
- Preserve the layered architecture boundaries
- Never introduce blocking operations on hot paths
- Maintain thread safety invariants
- Use existing error handling patterns
- Keep latency budget under 200μs total
- Follow the established data flow pipeline

Assistants MUST NOT:
- Add synchronous network calls
- Introduce new threading models
- Break the Transport→Dispatch→Cache→Sink pattern
- Modify the JWT authentication without understanding ES256/nonce requirements
- Add heavy logging on hot paths
- Change the LiveOrderBook dense format without GPU rendering consideration

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 9. Integration Points

## Upstream: Coinbase Advanced Trade WebSocket API
- ES256 JWT authentication required
- Channels: level2 (order book), market_trades
- Message types: snapshot, update, trade, subscriptions, error

## Downstream: GUI Rendering Pipeline
- Signals: tradeReceived(), liveOrderBookUpdated()
- Consumers: UnifiedGridRenderer, MarketDataPanel, etc
- All connections MUST be Qt::QueuedConnection

